Add jq 1.8.2 and a windows_arm64 platform

The bundled jq toolchain pins 1.7 and has no Windows arm64 platform, so
resolution fails on that host and takes unrelated targets with it: ours
surfaced through an oci image push.

jq publishes jq-windows-arm64.exe from 1.8.0 onward (jqlang/jq#3340), so
this adds the 1.8.2 hashes, a windows_arm64 entry, and moves the default
to 1.8.2, the first version carrying every platform listed here.

Integrity values were computed from the released binaries and match the
sha256sum.txt published alongside them.

diff --git a/lib/private/jq_toolchain.bzl b/lib/private/jq_toolchain.bzl
index f8cd0c7..04c9fb8 100644
--- a/lib/private/jq_toolchain.bzl
+++ b/lib/private/jq_toolchain.bzl
@@ -39,15 +39,30 @@ JQ_PLATFORMS = {
             "@platforms//cpu:x86_64",
         ],
     ),
+    "windows_arm64": struct(
+        release_platform = "windows-arm64",
+        compatible_with = [
+            "@platforms//os:windows",
+            "@platforms//cpu:arm64",
+        ],
+    ),
 }
 
-DEFAULT_JQ_VERSION = "1.7"
+DEFAULT_JQ_VERSION = "1.8.2"
 
 # https://github.com/stedolan/jq/releases
 #
 # The integrity hashes can be computed with
 # shasum -b -a 384 [downloaded file] | awk '{ print $1 }' | xxd -r -p | base64
 JQ_VERSIONS = {
+    "1.8.2": {
